<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via five-day fixed-system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via five-day fixed-system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system via a round of five-day fixed-system repurchase agreements on Thursday, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York confirmed.</p>
<p>An add had been expected by economists.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-1/2 percent, right at the Fed's current official target level.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663 ))</p>
